-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DISCLAIMER OF LIABILITY AND SERVICE TERMS FOR CHAT.JJPLZ.PARTY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

By using the hosted service at https://chat.jjplz.party or deploying this 
Software independently, you acknowledge and agree to the following terms:

1. END-TO-END ENCRYPTION & SECURITY:
   While the Software employs client-side End-to-End Encryption (E2EE) using 
   standard Web Crypto APIs (AES-GCM 256-bit), security depends heavily on user 
   practices (e.g., strength of the passphrase chosen, security of local 
   devices, browser updates). The maintainers do not guarantee absolute 
   invulnerability against local malware, device compromise, or user error.

2. PASSPHRASE RESPONSIBILITY:
   Encryption keys are derived locally in the user's browser and are NEVER 
   transmitted to or stored on the server. If you lose or misplace your 
   encryption passphrase, your encrypted messages and media cannot be recovered. 
   The operators of chat.jjplz.party cannot reset passphrases or recover data.

3. NO DATA GUARANTEE & EPHEMERAL STORAGE:
   The hosted application is designed for real-time ephemeral messaging. File 
   uploads (video/media) and chat buffers may be deleted, purged, or lost at 
   any time without prior notice due to server restarts, maintenance, or 
   storage limits. Do not use this service as a permanent storage facility.

4. ACCEPTABLE USE:
   You agree not to use the Software or hosted service for illegal activities, 
   malicious distribution, or activities that violate local or international 
   laws. The maintainers reserve the right to restrict service access, IP 
   addresses, or terminate rooms in cases of abuse or infrastructure disruption.

5. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY:
   Under no circumstances shall the developer(s) or operator(s) of 
   chat.jjplz.party be held liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, 
   consequential, or privacy-related damages resulting from the use or inability 
   to use this Software or service.
